course: dictionary
lesson: 7334
title: Planning: deciding before you act
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Planning means deciding and arranging what you will do, and how, before you do it. The clues are in the words around it. «Much housework is invisible, like booking appointments and planning meals.» Booking appointments is done ahead of time, so planning meals must mean deciding in advance what meals to make.
explain: Planning can also mean a plan or notes you make before you write, build or do something. Maya makes planning notes about the beginning, middle and end before she starts her story. Planning helps you finish well, because you know what to do next.
explain: Planning can be an official word too. «People must ask the council for planning permission before building something big, and neighbours can object.» Here planning means the process a town uses to decide what can be built, and it is not about your own to-do list.
fact: Planning means deciding and arranging what you will do, and how, before you do it.
fact: «Planning» can mean a plan or notes made before writing, building or doing something.
fact: «Planning permission» is the official process of deciding what can be built in a town.
fact: «Planning to» do something means you intend to do it.
fact: Planning is the -ing form of the verb plan: plan, plans, planned, planning.
exercise: «Much housework is invisible, like booking appointments and planning meals.» What does planning meals mean? | Buying a brand new kitchen | Throwing away old food | *Deciding in advance what meals to make | Eating every meal in a hurry
exercise: Nadia says, «I am planning to join the swimming club.» What does planning to mean here? | Never wanting to join the club | Having already joined the club | Forgetting the club exists | *Intending to join the club
exercise: «People must ask the council for planning permission before building something big.» What is planning permission? | Money given to builders | A picnic plan for the weekend | A ticket to a football match | *The official process of deciding what can be built in a town
test: Maya makes planning notes about the beginning, middle and end before she writes her story. What are her planning notes? | Shopping list for the week | A picture of a dragon | *A plan or notes made before writing | Money for the school trip
test: Which word is the -ing form of the verb plan? | *planning | plans | planned | plain
exam: «Revenge usually makes a fight bigger, so tell a teacher instead of planning payback.» What does planning payback mean here? | Asking a teacher for help with maths | Writing a story about a fight | *Deciding in advance how to get even with someone | Forgetting about the fight completely
